* pk_durable_write.dts -- AIF-156 two-run harness, RUN 1 of 2.
*
* THE QUESTION THIS PAIR EXISTS TO ASK, AND THE ONLY INSTRUMENT THAT CAN ASK IT.
* PKPOLICY proves the PRIMARY key is REFUSED on three write paths. It cannot
* prove the DECLARATION SURVIVES A RESTART, because a .dts runs in ONE process
* and the spec's own header says so under NOT CLAIMED. Until 2026-09-07 the
* designation lived in a process-local std::unordered_map -- unique_registry.cpp
* calls it "not persistent schema metadata" in its own boundary comment -- so it
* was forgotten at exit and a REPLACE in a fresh session overwrote the key IN
* SILENCE, on a build where all three arms read green.
*
* RUN 1 DECLARES AND WRITES. RUN 2 IS A SEPARATE PROCESS THAT NEVER REDECLARES.
* Nothing in this file asserts anything about durability: the whole claim is in
* run 2, and this run exists to leave a table behind with the designation
* stamped into its x64 header. Its guards are here so that a run 2 failure
* cannot be blamed on a fixture that was never built.
*
* THE KEY FIELD IS EMPNO AND THE SECOND FIELD IS SID, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE
* POINT OF THE SCHEMA. MEASURED 2026-09-08, on the earlier fixture whose key
* WAS named SID: run 2 appended a row and the key came out 3 in a process that
* had declared nothing, and it was read as proof that generation consults the
* stamped header. It was not. append_support.cpp::finalize_appended_record
* calls TWO generators in sequence -- generate_registered_uniques(), which asks
* unique_reg::list_unique_fields() and therefore the PROCESS MAP ONLY, and
* generate_sid_if_needed(), which asks nothing at all and fires whenever a
* field is literally NAMED "SID". The map was empty in run 2. The magic name
* minted the key. THE FIXTURE ANSWERED ITS OWN QUESTION.
*
* So SID stays in the table ON PURPOSE, as a LIVE CONTROL rather than as the
* subject. EMPNO is declared and stamped; SID is declared nowhere and is minted
* by name. One APPEND in run 2 writes both, in the same row, in the same call,
* and the difference between them isolates the one thing under test: whether
* key GENERATION reads the same authority key ENFORCEMENT reads. A control that
* rides in the same row as the arm cannot diverge from it for any other reason.
*
* PKDURABLE's own registry summary had already warned that this fixture's field
* name does hidden work -- the long-name hazard note, "SID is three characters,
* so this fixture CANNOT expose...". Same hazard, opposite consequence: that
* time the name would have hidden a mismatch, this time it manufactured a pass.
*
* DELIBERATELY NOT ERASED AT THE END. Every other fixture in this tree cleans up
* after itself; this one MUST outlive its process or there is nothing to reopen.
* Run 2 erases it.

SET TALK OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

SETPATH DBF D:\code\ccode\dottalkpp\data\DBF\SANDBOX
SETPATH INDEXES D:\code\ccode\dottalkpp\data\INDEXES\SANDBOX
SETPATH LMDB D:\code\ccode\dottalkpp\data\LMDB\SANDBOX

SET ALTERNATE TO D:\code\ccode\dottalkpp\data\tmp\pkdur_run1.alt
SET ALTERNATE ON

FORMULA "PKDUR-RUN1-BEGIN"

ERASE TABLE PKDUR CONFIRM

CREATE X64 PKDUR (EMPNO N(6,0), SID N(6,0), LNAME C(12))
CLOSE

SELECT 1
USE PKDUR

* The declaration under test. On a build that stamps the x64 header this writes
* X64_FIELD_FLAG_PRIMARY into EMPNO's X64FieldMetaEntry and
* DBF64_FLAG_HAS_RECID_PK into the table flags. On a build that does not, it
* only touches a map that dies with this process. NOTHING IS DECLARED ABOUT
* SID, here or anywhere -- that is what makes it a control.
SET UNIQUE FIELD EMPNO PRIMARY

APPEND
REPLACE LNAME WITH "ALPHA"
? "PKD_W1_first_key_is_1:" + (EMPNO = 1)

* PKD_W5 -- THE CONTROL IS ALIVE IN THE DECLARING PROCESS. The magic-name
* generator fires here too, so run 2's reading of SID is comparable to this one
* rather than to nothing. If this reads .F. the control is dead and run 2's
* discrimination is worthless -- which is a fixture failure, not a finding.
? "PKD_W5_undeclared_SID_minted_by_name:" + (SID = 1)

APPEND
REPLACE LNAME WITH "BETA"
? "PKD_W2_second_key_is_2:" + (EMPNO = 2)

* PKD_W3 -- the refusal works IN THIS PROCESS. Without this, a red in run 2
* cannot separate "the declaration did not survive" from "enforcement is broken
* on this build entirely", which are different findings with different fixes.
GO 1
REPLACE EMPNO WITH "2"
? "PKD_W3_refused_in_declaring_process:" + (EMPNO = 1)

* PKD_W4 -- the row run 2 will read is on disk and says what run 2 expects.
? "PKD_W4_row1_is_ALPHA:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) = "ALPHA")

CLOSE

FORMULA "PKDUR-RUN1-END"

SET ALTERNATE OFF
QUIT
